    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0080" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg30"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Tripp.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 85.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that Mr. Townsend’s
                    dispatch No. 86½, of the 1st instant, inclosing copies of correspondence
                    relative to the refusal of Mr. Schlessing, the U.S. consular agent at Haida, to
                    deliver certain property to the officers of the district court, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that Mr. Townsend’s course in regard to the matter in
                    question is fully approved by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
